+(def ^:private query-block-note
+  "How the insert operations make a Query block (patch 0050), shared by the four that take tree nodes."
+  (str "A node with a query field, or whose whole title is a ```query fence (any case) holding an EDN map (an advanced query), becomes a Query block, as the app's advanced query command makes one: tagged Query, with logseq.property/query holding the text as a Clojure code block, read back in the transaction, and marked with the hidden claudeQueryBlock property (true), which tells updateBlock that Claude made it; the property is created, hidden, on first use, and a property already in its way (another property titled claudeQueryBlock, or its ident held by a property of another type) refuses the call with 409 naming it. The map is {:query [:find … :where …]} with optional :inputs (a vector), :title (a string) and the flags :collapsed?, :group-by-page?, :remove-block-children? and :breadcrumb-show?; at most 4,000 characters."
+       " A fence-made block's title is \"\" and the response marks it converted: query; a field-made block keeps its title as a caption. Every Query block the call makes carries query (the stored text) in the response, also with verbose=false. A block reused by its uuid is left as it is."
+       " The query is checked as datalog_query checks a query before it runs: one EDN form, read-only, no rules (no :rules, % in :in or rule call), only the pure functions datalog_query allows, no cross product, at most 12 function bindings and 20 inputs, matching :in. :query must be a vector starting with :find, the only form the app runs, and :view and :result-transform are refused because they run as code in the app."
+       " A refused query answers 400 naming the node and the reason (blocks[0].children[1]: query: …, entries[2].blocks[0]: query: …) and writes nothing; so do a query field and a ```query fence on one node, a query with display-type or lang (fields or properties), a query with the Query, Code, Math or Quote tag, and a query field on an E2EE graph. A ```query fence whose body doesn't start with { (a simple query such as (task todo)) stays text, listed under kept (only an advanced query ({:query [...]}) becomes a Query block; a simple query stays text)."
+       " The query runs in the owner's app, not on the server: datalog_query's runtime caps (scan, join, row and the others) and its Private filter don't apply there, so a costly query can slow the page that holds it, and its results can list Private blocks in the app (the connector never reads them)."))
 
